udgment inputs, and replay derives them. The destination still serializes one judge/publication, host reads do not invent attempt outcomes, uncertain effects remain owned, and refused withdraw changes no destination state. Directory/register/destination rules and extents rows stay distinct from source adapters and deployment. Design versions, adopted standing, proposals and historical corrections are explicit.\n\nSecurity: authority cannot come from caller-supplied authors/controller claims, a session bearer, a receipt label or elapsed time. The exception only replaces the rules extent's reviews under its declared conditions, leaving checks, other extents and grants intact. Observations must bind repository/scope/incarnation/key/member/head/window and complete retention; a fixed relationship alone is not a witness that the destination obtained it. Device/session residual-read policy, token revocation, worker standing, pins, custody and unknown outside effects keep their separate rules and owners. Real host/token/credential/checker/browser/device/recovery/deployment evidence is not supplied here.\n\nSimplification and value: restoring one existing predicate with explicit current overrides avoids a second author-only policy and preserves the main one-person-directing-agents journey. Form15 should use the existing observation/history/replay path for positive exceptions and negative independence decisions, with a complete count/byte budget. Product views must distinguish a policy-permitted but unbuilt relation, missing evidence, unmet review, not-reserved and a completed reservation. Per-extent actions and versioned marks preserve customization. Throughput may improve within those responsibilities; it cannot abandon unknown effects or weaken retained evidence.\n\nCoverage: fresh collective FULL all three current bodies, including unchanged facts: 1,591,202 UTF-8 bytes, 17,159 LF. Complete native U3 against exact parent: 72,008 bytes, 791 LF (facts delta empty). Core rea